+### Spatially-variable genes (SVGs) {#sec-crs-svg}
+
+SVGs are usually identified integrating gene expression measurements with spatial coordinates, either with or without predefined spatial domains.
+SVGs approaches can be broadly categorized into three types: overall SVGs, spatial domain-specific SVGs, and cell type-specific SVGs [@Yan2024]. 
 
-Here, we demonstrate a short example showing how to identify a set of top SVGs using `r BiocStyle::Biocpkg("nnSVG")` [@Weber2023], which is available through Bioconductor and can be easily integrated into Bioconductor-based workflows.
